      "text": "Let the cost of a pen be $x$ cents and the cost of a pencil be $y$ cents.\nFrom the given information, we have the following system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n4x+3y &= 224, \\\\\n2x+5y &= 154.\n\\end{align*}\nSolving the second equation for $x$, we get $x = 77-2.5y$.\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we find that $3y=224-220$, so $y=\\boxed{8}$.\n\nWhat is the product of the roots of the equation $x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0$?\n\nWe can factor the quadratic as $(x-2)(x-3) = 0$.\nTherefore, the roots are $x = 2$ and $x = 3$.\nThe product of the roots is $2 \\times 3 = \\boxed{6}$.\nThe answer is: 6",
